{"skill":{"slug":"tiangong-notebooklm-cli","displayName":"NotebookLM CLI"},"version":{"version":"0.1.1","createdAt":1770454856990,"changelog":"remove tiangong workspace relation","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1126,"sha256":"a955524c02813fa92a4217006e66ab0e6de6054a5bee465b85eb192379ba11a3","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/notebooklm.mjs","size":902,"sha256":"66b47d85c1ae14d0db0dfa9a3a235b4279666e181abffbe3f714f1528c2cd931","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"references/cli-commands.md","size":4554,"sha256":"e27adefe6b8c94993469eadf5c32baae5ccbeb79d694d13f7d46e4dfd69fe90e","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1880,"sha256":"d9f5577c719e6edfc1ddfc9824fc098d5694ba1d60684074a042f868146af897","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022508992,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d180d4d9844a6e04c47b5f2c399ca56b26f596ef1d3d1654a064da5fe039312a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d180d4d9844a6e04c47b5f2c399ca56b26f596ef1d3d1654a064da5fe039312a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: tiangong-notebooklm-cli\nVersion: 0.1.1\n\nThe skill bundle acts as a thin wrapper for the `notebooklm` CLI tool. The `scripts/notebooklm.mjs` file uses `node:child_process.spawnSync` to execute the `notebooklm` command, passing all arguments directly. This is a legitimate and common pattern for CLI wrappers, and arguments are passed as an array, mitigating shell injection vulnerabilities within the wrapper itself. The `SKILL.md` and `references/cli-commands.md` files provide clear, functional instructions for using the wrapper without any evidence of prompt injection attempts or instructions for malicious behavior. There is no indication of data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, or other malicious intent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160176100},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":21,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789022508992},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent NotebookLM CLI wrapper, but it exposes authenticated notebook deletion and public sharing commands without enough safety scoping or privacy warnings.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of an authenticated external NotebookLM account is expected for this purpose, but prompts, sources, notes, artifacts, and sharing changes may affect external account data.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No hidden installer or remote payload retrieval was found; the included script only invokes `notebooklm` from PATH with the supplied arguments.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The command catalog includes destructive `--yes` deletion commands and sharing commands that can add editors or enable public access, but it does not clearly warn users about irreversible data loss or exposure of notebook contents.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill itself does not create persistence or privilege escalation, but it relies on the user's existing NotebookLM authentication/session and documents commands that can modify account-hosted content.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The wrapper's capabilities align with its stated purpose: it forwards user-selected commands to the existing `notebooklm` CLI for auth, notebooks, chat, sources, notes, sharing, research, and artifacts.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing if you use NotebookLM with private, regulated, or business-sensitive material. Only run deletion, sharing, public access, export, and import commands when you have verified the target notebook or recipient and understand the account-level impact.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The authenticated NotebookLM data flow is expected for this wrapper, but the artifact does not sufficiently disclose the sensitivity of sending notebook prompts, sources, notes, and artifacts to the external service.\n[SQP-2] expected: Notebook, source, note, and artifact deletion commands are purpose-aligned, but examples using `--yes` are under-scoped because the catalog lacks caution about irreversible removal and target verification.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sharing commands are part of notebook management, but enabling public access and editor permissions without privacy guidance is a material review concern.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The fixed `language set zh_Hans` example is a documentation quality issue rather than a security driver; it does not affect the final verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022508992}}}}}